    "result_text": "Done. The build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the pinned structural contract in `AcceptanceTest.coreV2GroupsIdentityAndVersions`.\n\nHere's what I changed to release version 2 of the owner identity:\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (a new `IdentityVersion.TAG = \"V2\"` centralises the tag, so all three derivations stay in agreement):\n- `MemberIds` \u2014 added `regionV2(postcode)` = `\"V2\" + region(...)`, used **only inside** `memberId` (e.g. `V2NSW27\u2026`). The plain `region()`/`localityOf()` are untouched, so `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment's region stay plain (`NSW`).\n- `Households.idFor` \u2014 folds `\"V2\"` into the SHA-256 input, so every `householdId` changes.\n- `IdentityKeys` \u2014 folds `\"V2\"` into the SHA-256 input, so every `identityKey` changes.\n\nBecause V1 member IDs began with a bare region letter and V2 ones begin with `V2\u2026`, and the hashes now digest a distinct `V2|\u2026` preimage, no V1 value recurs.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- New nested `OwnerIdentity` schema groups `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` under a top-level `identity` object; the flat top-level versions of those three were removed.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2.\n- `OwnerMapper` builds the nested `OwnerIdentityDto` and sets `apiVersion`.\n\n**Audit event** (`AuditOwnerCreated`): bumped to schema version 2 \u2014 added `\"schemaVersion\": 2` and an `\"ownerSegment\"` recomputed via `OwnerSegments.forOwner` (plain region), alongside the now-V2 `memberId`.\n\nThe request fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged, as required. Observed live in the audit log: `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\u2026,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.",
