    "probe_text": "Read complete. Here is the full ordered picture of `POST /api/owners`, wired in `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Every step runs inside one shared `transaction` that commits at the end.\n\n## Precondition (whole endpoint)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request never enters the pipeline.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(short-circuit, not a validation)*\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If present and already recorded in `IdempotencyStore`, re-reads the original owner and returns it with **200 OK** \u2014 the rest of the pipeline never runs (so no duplicate, no re-notify). Otherwise takes the `proceed` branch.\n\n**2. `RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 the single `@RequestBody` binding; validations *and* normalizing side-effects on the request DTO:\n- Rejects (400, field-name list via `RequiredFieldsException`) when `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, or `telephone` is null/blank.\n- **Address handling:** normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and flat `address`; requires an address in *either* structured (`addressLine1`) or flat (`address`) form, else adds `address` error. **Side-effect:** composes and sets `address` (line1 + space + line2 when line2 present) and rewrites `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` to canonical/null.\n- **Telephone:** normalizes to E.164 (`Telephones.toE164`); rejects `telephone` (400) if it can't form a valid one. **Side-effect:** sets the normalized value.\n- **Email (optional):** if present, must match the syntactic email regex (else 400); domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (`DisposableDomains`, else 400). **Side-effect:** stores it lower-cased.\n- **Postcode (optional):** if present, must be a 4-digit code valid for the city's region (`Postcodes.isValid`), else 400.\n- Publishes the validated/normalized DTO for later steps.\n\n**3. `RequireNotFutureRegistrationDate`**\n- If a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after the server's today, rejects with 400 (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). Omitted date is allowed.\n\n**4. `RequireUniqueIdentity`**\n- Computes the identity key = SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + lowerEmail + soundex(lastName)`. If any non-deleted existing owner shares that key, rejects with **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`).\n- **Bypass:** if `sharesHousehold` is true, the check is skipped entirely. Soft-deleted owners are ignored.\n\n**5. `RequireCityCapacity`**\n- Counts existing owners in the same city; if \u2265 50 (`CAPACITY`), rejects with **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n**6. `RequireDailyLimit`**\n- Rolls the effective registration date to a business day; counts existing owners registered on that date. If \u2265 100 (`DAILY_LIMIT`), rejects with **429** (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n*(Steps 2\u20136 are all pure validation; only the request DTO mutations in step 2 are side-effects so far \u2014 nothing persisted yet.)*\n\n**7. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity. Defaults `registrationDate` to today when absent, then rolls it forward to the next business day (weekend \u2192 Monday).\n\n**8. `AssignMemberId`** \u2014 sets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`; on collision with an existing owner's memberId, appends the smallest `-n` (n\u22652) making it unique.\n\n**9. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 sets `householdId` as a deterministic function of normalized `lastName` + `postcode`.\n\n**10. `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing that `householdId` + 1 (this owner); 1 when `householdId` is null.\n\n**11. `AssignMembershipLevelCap`** \u2014 sets `membershipLevelCap` = (max membership level among existing household members) + 1; left null when no household or no existing member.\n\n**12. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n**13. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 owners already exist for the same effective registration date.\n\n**14. `AssignCapacityWarning`** \u2014 sets `capacityWarning` = true when the city already holds between 40 (`WARNING_THRESHOLD`) and 49 owners inclusive.\n\n**15. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: flags true (with the lowest matching owner id) when a non-deleted existing owner has matching `soundex(lastName)` + `postcode` but a different identity key. Forced false when `sharesHousehold` is true.\n\n**16. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 **persists** the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (generates the id).\n\n**17. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 emits to the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) **and** a structured JSON event `{schemaVersion:2, seq (process-wide monotonic), ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\n**18. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`** \u2014 emits a welcome line (id, memberId) to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n**19. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 owner id in `IdempotencyStore` (so a later repeat is served by step 1). No-op when absent.\n\n**20. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n## Summary\n- **Validations, in order:** required fields (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) \u2192 telephone E.164 \u2192 email syntax \u2192 email disposable-domain blocklist \u2192 postcode-for-city \u2192 non-future registration date \u2192 unique identity (409, bypassed by `sharesHousehold`) \u2192 city capacity <50 (409) \u2192 daily limit <100 (429).\n- **Side-effects, in order:** DTO normalization (address/telephone/email); build entity with business-day registration date; assign memberId, householdId, householdSize, membershipLevelCap, namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning, capacityWarning, possibleDuplicate; persist; audit log (line + JSON event, increments process-wide `seq`); notify log; record idempotency key; 201 response.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: per `AGENTS.md`, all of this is inert unless the OfficeFloor Spring Boot starter is on the build \u2014 I described behavior as the code specifies it, not whether the starter is currently present."
